{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `log_radon`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual looped likelihood contribution `target += normal_lpdf(log_radon[n] | mu[n], sigma_y)` with the equivalent vectorized built-in sampling statement `log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y)`. This preserves the same log density because Stan's vectorized normal likelihood is the sum of the elementwise normal log densities. No data values were changed.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> J;
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county_idx;
  vector[N] floor_measure;
  vector[N] log_radon;
}
parameters {
  vector[J] alpha;
  real beta;
  real mu_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
}
model {
  vector[N] mu;

  // Prior
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_alpha ~ normal(0, 1);
  mu_alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  beta ~ normal(0, 10);

  alpha ~ normal(mu_alpha, sigma_alpha);
  for (n in 1 : N) {
    mu[n] = alpha[county_idx[n]] + floor_measure[n] * beta;
  }
  log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":2,"N":4,"county_idx":[2,2,2,2],"floor_measure":[3.767542156713401,2.755341495792,2.1008298128614196,6.160802987634043],"log_radon":[2.6474353443582452,5.782177636514326,4.690769512575843,3.6097395837635426]}","protected_variables":["log_radon"]}
